# Secrets
#
# Nothing here exists yet, and that is the point: these rules are in place
# BEFORE the file is created, because the dangerous window is between writing a
# credential and noticing it was staged. Checked when added: no tracked file
# matches any of these patterns, so nothing was un-tracked by adding them.
#
# .streamlit/secrets.toml is the one that matters most. That folder IS tracked,
# on purpose, because config.toml holds the theme and the app opens in the wrong
# colours without it. So the folder is not ignored wholesale and the secrets file
# has to be named on its own line. It is Streamlit's standard home for API keys
# and database passwords, and every tutorial tells you to put credentials there.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# .env is already listed under Environments below, but the bare name does not
# match .env.local or .env.production, which are the ones a framework generates.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private keys and certificates.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Where git, curl and the GitHub CLI cache a token. s06_publish reads
# GITHUB_TOKEN from the environment and never writes it to disk, but a tool run
# by hand in this folder can leave one of these behind.
.netrc
_netrc
.git-credentials

