# --- F1 Reality Check: project-specific ---

# Database backups (the *.db rule above does NOT catch these)
*.db.backup*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Local tool config
.claude/

# GitHub Codespaces / VS Code container definition. Generated by the Streamlit
# starter template, never used: this project is developed locally against a
# pinned Anaconda 3.13 environment, and the file pinned 3.11. Ignored so that
# reopening the project in an editor that offers to add one cannot put it back.
.devcontainer/

# Pipeline logs
logs/

# Scratch
tree.txt

# outputs/ no longer exists. The bundle moved to dashboard/data/ and the coverage
# snapshot to pipeline/, where it is tracked on purpose: it is the gate's baseline
# and a baseline that is not committed resets to nothing on a fresh clone.
# outputs/analysis/ is still created on demand by
# `s05b_prescriptive.py --tables perfect_lap`, and caught by the *.csv rule above.

# Dashboard bundle. dashboard.db is caught by the *.db rule above; the gzip is
# not, and it must stay out of git. s06 publishes it as a GitHub Release asset
# precisely so a 12 MB file rewritten every run never enters the history.
#
# Matched on the filename, not on a folder, because the bundle now lives beside
# the app in dashboard/data/ rather than in outputs/. A path-anchored rule
# silently stops protecting anything the moment the file moves, which is how a
# 12 MB binary would end up committed. The data/ rule further up ignores that
# folder whole, so the bundle is covered twice over on purpose.
*.db.gz
*.gz

# gold_f1.db is caught by the *.db rule above. It is 100 MB and fully derived,
# so it is rebuilt rather than stored: pipeline/s07_build_gold.py --execute